Good questions.  I don't think practices have evolved much in using any 
type of MI methods, but these would be good additions.  The 2 issues your 
suggestions imply address (1) replicability of the imputation model 
results (in which case we need to know the options chosen), and (2) model 
dependence (for which we need to know how much imputating was done overall 
or by variable).  Finding ways of meeting these 2 rules seem worthwhile in 
any modeling exercise, including multiple imputation.

